A stopped player hides the module, as no player does. Upstream skips the
update instead, so the last title stays on the bar as if still playing: a
browser tab keeps its player after a video ends (LinkedIn's feed, say), and
clicking the frozen title does nothing. install.sh applies patches/waybar/ on
every machine.

--- a/src/modules/mpris/mpris.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/mpris/mpris.cpp
@@ -849,7 +849,9 @@
   }
 
   if (info.status == PLAYERCTL_PLAYBACK_STATUS_STOPPED) {
-    spdlog::debug("mpris[{}]: player stopped, skipping update", info.name);
+    spdlog::debug("mpris[{}]: player stopped, hiding", info.name);
+    event_box_.set_visible(false);
+    ALabel::update();
     return;
   }
 
